---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { company, legal } from '../data/site'

/**
 * These terms deliberately match what the marketing page promises. If you
 * change the commercial terms in `site.ts`, change them here the same day —
 * a customer who spots the page and the contract disagreeing will assume the
 * more expensive one is the real one, and they will be right to.
 *
 * TODO before you run paid ads: have somebody qualified read this.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  heading="Terms of service"
  intro="The terms we work under. They are short on purpose, and they say the same thing the rest of the site says."
>
  <h2>Who these terms are with</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover services provided by {company.legalName}, operating from{' '}
    {company.location}, to the business that engages us. They apply from the
    point we begin setting up your service.
  </p>

  <h2>What we provide</h2>
  <p>
    Phone answering, lead follow-up, and appointment booking, configured for
    your business and run on your behalf. The specific scope for your account is
    whatever we agree in writing before setup — the descriptions on this website
    are what the service does generally, not a fixed list of what your account
    includes.
  </p>

  <h2>Setup</h2>
  <p>
    Configuration, test calls, calendar connection and the tuning that follows
    go-live are included at no extra charge. Setup needs your input: what you do,
    the area you cover, your prices, and what counts as urgent. We cannot build
    an accurate assistant without it, and delays in getting it are the usual
    reason a go-live slips.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees and your rate</h2>
  <p>
    Fees are agreed in writing before your service begins and billed monthly in
    advance. The rate you start on is the rate you keep for as long as your
    service runs continuously. If our standard pricing rises later, it applies
    to new customers, not to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Plans are sized to your call volume. If your usage moves well beyond the
    band your plan covers, we will tell you before anything changes and agree a
    plan that fits, rather than issuing a surprise invoice.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Month to month, with no minimum term and no notice period. Tell us you want
    to stop and we will stop at the end of your current paid month. There is no
    cancellation fee and no charge for exporting your own data.
  </p>

  <h2>Your number and your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your phone number remains yours throughout and is unaffected by leaving.
    Call recordings, transcripts, contact records and booking history belong to
    you. You may export them at any time, including on the way out, and ask us
    to delete our copies afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2>What the service can and cannot do</h2>
  <p>
    The assistant is configured not to quote prices, commit to timescales, or
    answer technical questions it has not been given answers to. It takes a
    message or transfers the call instead. It is a well-built system rather than
    a person, and like any system it can misunderstand a caller. You keep
    control: you see every booking as it happens and can change or cancel it.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not guarantee a particular number of bookings, a particular revenue
    figure, or uninterrupted service. The calculator on our website is
    arithmetic on figures you enter, and is an illustration of what missed calls
    may be costing you — not a forecast, a promise, or a projection of results.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and dependencies</h2>
  <p>
    The service relies on third-party telephony, voice, and calendar providers,
    and on your own phone service and internet connection. Outages in any of
    those can interrupt it. We will tell you when we know about a problem and
    fix what is ours to fix.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give us accurate information about your business, and tell us when it changes</li>
    <li>Hold the rights to the phone number and calendar you ask us to connect</li>
    <li>Comply with the laws that apply to your own customer communications</li>
    <li>
      Tell us before go-live if you handle medical, clinical, or other regulated
      personal information, so it can be dealt with properly rather than
      discovered later
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    Our liability in connection with the service is limited to the fees you paid
    us in the three months before the claim arose. We are not liable for lost
    profits, lost business, or indirect losses. Nothing here limits liability
    that cannot lawfully be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {legal.governingLaw}.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms in a way that affects you, we will email you before
    the change takes effect. Continuing to use the service after that means you
    accept it; if you would rather not, cancel, and nothing further is owed.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Anything about these terms goes to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>, or call{' '}
    <a href={`tel:${company.phones[0].raw}`}>{company.phones[0].display}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
